  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU needs the optional RS485 interface (485 in the order code); the USB port also speaks Modbus RTU. Functions 03, 05 and 06; writes with address 0 are broadcast.",
    "8 data bits, 1 stop bit, no parity. The manual does not give the factory address or baud rate: check the addr and bavd screens.",
    "Every register is a signed 16-bit value. Registers 12 and up can be read and written; most registers below 12 are read-only.",
    "Process value, setpoints, limits, offset and alarm setpoints are integers in display units with the decimals of register 30 (dppo): 0 = 3 decimals, 3 = none.",
    "A write outside the allowed range is not refused: the controller stores the maximum allowed value and returns it.",
    "The ramp and soak programs (registers 73 to 240: events, tolerance, link, times and setpoints of programs 1 to 7) are not listed.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "unit_id": 1,
  "databits": 8,
  "parity": "N",
  "stopbits": 1,
  "byte_order": "big",
